PSS Central Institute of Vocational Education, Bhopal
Genesis
The Pandit Sunderlal Sharma Central Institute of Vocational Education (PSSCIVE) is an apex research and development organization in the field of vocational education.
It is a constituent unit of National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT), established in 1993 by the Ministry of Education (MoE), Government of India.
The Institute has a picturesque 38-acre campus at Shyamla Hills in Bhopal.
It comprises six academic disciplines, namely Agriculture and Animal Husbandry, Business and Commerce, Engineering and Technology, Health and Paramedical Science, Home Science and Hospitality Management and Humanities, Science, Education and Research with 05 Centres
The Institute is also a UNEVOC (International Project on Technical and Vocational Education) Network Centre in India, which coordinates all the activities, including communication with UNESCO-UNEVOC International Centre, Bonn, Germany.
Through the network, the Centre shares knowledge and experiences related to all aspects of VET, exchange country experiences, and discuss issues of common relevance.
The institute offers quality training programs in vocational pedagogy and a wide range of subjects for key functionaries in vocational education and vocational teachers.
The highly qualified team of the institute has excellent professional skills and experience which is essential for providing classroom teaching and training.
The institute has led the way in rapid growth in the field of vocational education, often responding positively to the changing needs of the industry and at times leading to significant changes in the field of vocational education.
The development of the Institute over the past twenty five years has seen various challenges and constraints, but these also serve as opportunities to explore new horizons and to work on the possibilities of restructuring strategies to meet the skill needs of people both locally and globally.
Have also worked in Canvas.
Employability Skills
Employability skills have been included as a common core of curriculum across all vocational subjects from Grades IX to XII to empower students for work and life.
