Collection-
The Allahabad Museum houses art, antiquities, paintings, sculptures, coins, ceramics, archaeological objects, illustrated manuscripts, edicts, decorative artifacts, weapons, textiles, specimens of natural history, photographs, prints and personal collections, especially of Gandhi There is a diverse and rich collection of artifacts related to , Nehru and the literary personalities of Allahabad such as Sumitranandan Pant, Suryakant Tripathi 'Nirala', Premchandra, Mahadevi Verma.
Apart from displaying the artifacts in 16 galleries, temporary exhibitions of artefacts from the protected collection focusing on various subjects are organized from time to time in the Anand Kumaraswamy Memorial Hall and Central Hall for the rotation of the artifacts.
